<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI28-RSH-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI28-RSH-002" ;
  triage:title "Mutex poisoning silently swallowed in 4 bookkeeping helpers" ;
  triage:description "Four bookkeeping helper functions in peer_drain_coordinator.rs silently ignore mutex poisoning (errors from Mutex::lock() when the lock-holding thread panicked): release(), mark_generation_observed(), generation_changed(), and reset_backoff(). When any of these helpers encounter a poisoned lock (due to a panic in another thread holding the lock), they use `.unwrap_or_else()` or similar constructs to swallow the error and continue. This creates a silent failure mode: a poisoned slot lock permanently wedges that slot's state at running=true with zero observability or logging. The host loses the ability to schedule further recovery for that peer and silently stops attempting delivery. This is particularly dangerous because: (1) the lock poisoning is silent (no error is logged), (2) the coordinator worker thread can panic for legitimate reasons (e.g., a computation overflow in backoff math, or an internal invariant violation), and (3) the operator has no way to detect that recovery has stalled for a specific peer. Fix required: propagate poisoning errors as real failures (log with context, mark the slot as poisoned/stalled, and potentially take recovery offline for that peer), or at minimum log a critical-level error every time a poisoning is encountered." ;
  triage:category "Service-Hardening" ;
  triage:severity "Important" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T22:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "Independently re-verified against real code on feature/pAI-s28-bounded-peer-recovery current head c0445b1a. All 4 cited functions (release() line 163, mark_generation_observed() line 172, generation_changed() line 179, reset_backoff() line 186) now return Result<_, AtmError> and propagate poisoning via self.slots()? instead of swallowing it with unwrap_or_default()/similar." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S8 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T16:53:36Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-25T09:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI28-RSH-002/pAI-s28/1> ;
